WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
when working with documents there may be

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.450
some information now you wish to display

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.760
consistently throughout the documents so

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.040
if you had 20 pages you may want to have

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:15.179
the date and the company logo on every

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.379
page and also a page numbers to do that

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:19.199
you would use the headers and footers

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:21.750
section of the document now the headers

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:23.820
and footers aren't displayed by default

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:27.029
you have to actually access them to

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.619
enter the information so to do that as

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:31.170
you can see I have a blank document on

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.329
the screen and there are two ways of

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:37.110
accessing the headers and footers you

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:39.420
can go to the insert tab which brings up

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:44.850
the insert toolbar and then select

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:46.410
header and footer and alternatively you

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.329
can just click in the document and if I

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.219
just double click at the very very top

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.440
it will automatically open the header

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.469
and then I can just say what I wish to

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:58.680
put in to the header and for an example

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:02.039
I'm going to insert the date and time so

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.989
if I select the date and time icon going

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:06.659
to select which format that I wanted to

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:10.979
display in and I'll select the second

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:16.439
one down so I select on there and that

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:17.580
will give me the date in the header the

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:20.130
beauty of using the headers and footers

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.890
is that when you make changes are you

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.810
move further down the page and the

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.920
document size increases so far scroll

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.600
down and just move on to another page as

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.590
you can see it's all a muddle the end of

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:37.590
the date on to that page similarly if I

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.420
wish to add pH numbers I would just

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:42.689
scroll to the bottom of the document and

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.119
again I can go to the insert tab or I

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:47.040
can just double click right at the very

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:50.280
bottom of the document which will open

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:53.909
the footer and then a canard pH number

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.530
so the select page number and then I

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:58.950
would obviously a select the alignment

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:01.110
so I do want Elaine to the right center

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.950
or left and I'm going to go for the

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:07.740
center select or care and that will

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:10.080
insert a page number into the footer and

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.960
as you can see that is carried through

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:16.180
on every page

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.160
you can't access the head doesn't foot

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.780
us at anytime so I can click away from

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.450
that and then work on my document

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.730
perhaps I wanted to make a change to the

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:27.400
deed format so I could just double click

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.830
back into that highlight the deed form

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.250
up and select a different way of

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:35.380
displaying it select or care and that

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.750
will change that and again if I wanted

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.250
to change how the footer or the page

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.260
number in the footer is displayed

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:48.100
I could double click in the footer

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:50.920
highlight the number and select page

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.380
number maybe that I want to right align

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:56.020
that select your care and then will

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:58.510
automatically right align it you can't

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:02.730
also insert images on other information

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.730
into the header as required